# the worked example for the drawn horse - the debugger's second act.
#
# the trace is the skeleton; this is the animal. every state the horse panel
# embodies arrives here as a chord, and each one is cited, because a pose
# that cannot be cited is decoration, and decoration is a bug.
#
#   ^ ears forward   head ~0    lids AU143 ^       contented - lids droop is
#                                                 the relaxed/dozing end of
#                                                 the ethogram (Lewis et al.
#                                                 2025; lids coded in EquiFACS)
#   _ ears back _                                 agonistic (EAD103, EquiFACS)
#                                                 - not attending, so the
#                                                 drawn horse dims + retreats
#   ^ ears divided   head ~-0.3 _                 divided - one ear each way
#                                                 (EAD103L / EAD103R); the two
#                                                 eyes look different ways
#                                                 (laterality, GRAMMAR.md 12g)
#   ^ ears forward   head ~0.85 ^                 head high - the horse rears
#                                                 (head height is part of the
#                                                 attention display, Wathan &
#                                                 McComb 2014)
#   ^ ears forward   head ~-0.9 ^                 head low - the horse sinks
#   ^ ears forward   nostrils AD38   tail ~-0.7 ^  flared nostrils + low tail:
#                                                 arousal display (ethogram)
#   ^ ears forward   tension ~0.8   tail ~0.6 ^    tense, tail raised: the
#                                                 reinforcement spine (applied
#                                                 animal behaviour science
#                                                 2025) and a raised carriage
#
# run it in the playground and watch the horse: it stands contented, flattens
# and vanishes into the corner, splits its attention, rears, sinks, flares,
# and braces - and the trace beside it tells the same story in frames.
#
# the debugger cites: Wathan & McComb 2014, Wathan et al. 2015 EquiFACS,
# Lewis et al. 2025 ethogram, GRAMMAR.md 4 and 12g.

@ storm  12  right bias

band moods

    context field
        hears snort
            ^ ears forward   nostrils AD38   tension ~0.1 ^
            release 1

    lead mare show
        # 1 - contented. relaxed head, drooping lids.
        ^ ears forward   head ~0   lids AU143 ^
        snort

        # 2 - both ears flattened. agonistic (EAD103). not attending.
        _ ears back _
        snort

        # 3 - divided attention: one ear forward, one back.
        ^ ears divided   head ~-0.3 _
        snort

        # 4 - head high: the horse rears.
        ^ ears forward   head ~0.85 ^
        snort

        # 5 - head low: the horse sinks.
        ^ ears forward   head ~-0.9 ^
        snort

        # 6 - arousal: flared nostrils, low tail.
        ^ ears forward   nostrils AD38   tail ~-0.7 ^
        snort

        # 7 - tense, tail raised.
        ^ ears forward   tension ~0.8   tail ~0.6 ^
        snort
        release